


   =====( ConvertUsers V1.00 )========================================


        Trion 'ConvertUsers' Utility.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '95-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================

   This utility was written to convert the Userdatabase between
   version. Which is more practicall than having to delete
   the entire userbase when installing a new version.

   At this moment it is only needed to convert the database from
   version 0.62 or earlier. In version 0.62 there was more space
   needed for a couple of variables. Also there are 64 empty
   bytes added at the conversion. So there is enough room for
   expansion for a long time. And this converter doesn't has
   to be extended soon.

   Note that each userfile is started with a userfile version byte
   so the converter knows which files it has to convert and can't
   scramble a userfile by mistake by converting a file twice
   when it was ran to often, also this makes it easier for
   future extensions.


   Note that the BBS programm itself checks if a user file
   is of the rigth version. If it is to old it will write a
   message to shell that you have to use convertusers.

   Before you start converting make sure the BBS isn't running
   so there are no userfiles in use at this time.
   (Run the "Trion:down" script to make sure).

   To convert users type "convert OK".
   At this time your users are converted, so make sure
   you run a NEW version of the BBS after conversion.
   
   Note that this programm only works if you type "OK"
   on the commandline. This is to make sure you don't
   accidently convert users with the Resource Manager
   and the BBS nodes active.

   Note that you should make a backup of the "trion:users/"
   directory before use .. so you could use old versions of
   the BBS if the new one doesn't work properly.
   Do I have to mention you always should have a backup of
   all the data and configuration files of the BBS ?
   It is a lot easier to copy a few config files from disk
   than to invent them from scratch.

